{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2420","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2420","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2420\",\"parent_revision\":\"d97039ccbabb804b27d7395bb21e416922ebb3334d17aaecd846156a5852d365\",\"root_revision\":\"d97039ccbabb804b27d7395bb21e416922ebb3334d17aaecd846156a5852d365\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\ncomplete-implementation applies status:verified to the backlog item but never closes the GitHub issue. After the PR is merged the session ends and the issue stays open indefinitely.\\n\\nThe current workflow relies on the user (or a follow-up session) to call `/dh:work-backlog-item resolve` manually, which is fragile and often skipped.\\n\\nThe fix must use `backlog_close` or `backlog_resolve` via the backlog MCP server as the final step of complete-implementation \u2014 NOT a GitHub-specific \\\"Closes #N\\\" annotation in the PR body or commit message. The PR annotation approach is GitHub-only and doesn't work for beads/sqlite/other backends. The MCP call is backend-agnostic.\\n\\nProposed final step addition to complete-implementation skill:\\nAfter the status:verified label is applied (Step 6 of Proportional Quality Gates, or equivalent in the SAM path), call:\\n  mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__backlog_resolve(selector=\\\"#{issue_number}\\\", reason=\\\"Implementation complete \u2014 PR merged, AC verified PASS\\\")\\n\\nThis transitions the item from in-progress \u2192 resolved, closes the GitHub issue (or equivalent per backend), and removes the in-progress label. It is the only backend-agnostic closure mechanism.\\n\\nState machine reference: in-progress \u2192 resolved trigger is /work-backlog-item resolve --reason, but complete-implementation should call the equivalent MCP operation directly since it already has the issue_number from context.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: fix: complete-implementation final step must close issue via backlog MCP, not GitHub-specific Closes\\nDate: 2026-05-23\\nGoal: Add backend-agnostic issue closure via backlog_resolve MCP call as the final step of complete-implementation, replacing/supplementing the GitHub-specific \\\"Fixes #NNN\\\" commit annotation.\\nConditions:\\n1. Location of complete-implementation SKILL.md | Status: AVAILABLE\\n   Evidence: plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md verified present\\n2. Current final step behavior (only Fixes #NNN in commit message, no backlog_resolve call) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n   Evidence: grep confirms no backlog_resolve/backlog_close calls in SKILL.md; only \\\"Fixes #NNN\\\" in commit message body\\n3. backlog_resolve MCP tool signature | Status: AVAILABLE\\n   Evidence: mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__backlog_resolve loaded in session; accepts selector, reason params\\n4. State machine transition in-progress \u2192 resolved via backlog_resolve | Status: AVAILABLE\\n   Evidence: documented in item description; backlog_update(status=\\\"in-progress\\\") already confirmed working\\n5. Correct insertion point for fix (after \\\"Apply status:verified Label\\\" section, before \\\"Final Step: Commit\\\") | Status: AVAILABLE\\n   Evidence: SKILL.md sections read; \\\"Apply status:verified Label\\\" \u2192 \\\"Final Step: Commit and Push\\\" is the exact insertion gap\\n6. Backend-agnostic requirement (MCP call works for GitHub + beads + sqlite) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n   Evidence: item description explicitly states this; backlog_resolve is in BacklogBackend Protocol, not GitHub-specific\\nAVAILABLE count: 6\\nDERIVABLE count: 0\\nMISSING count: 0\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **complete-implementation final step must close issue via backlog mcp, not github-specific closes** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session investigation: complete-implementation #2415 QG loop \u2014 issue #2415 remained open after PR #2417 merged\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-23)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n**Reproducibility**: Deterministic \u2014 every invocation of `/complete-implementation #N` that succeeds leaves the issue open.\\n\\n**Reproduction steps**:\\n1. Run `/complete-implementation #N` on any open issue with completed implementation\\n2. Quality gates pass, `status:verified` label is applied\\n3. Final step commits with `Fixes #NNN` in commit body\\n4. Check GitHub issue #N \u2014 it remains **open**\\n5. For beads backend: `Fixes #NNN` is omitted entirely \u2014 issue stays open with no closure mechanism at all\\n\\n**Context from which bug was discovered**: Issue #2415 remained open after PR #2417 merged (session 2026-05-22)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n**Priority**: P1\\n**Rationale**: Every completed implementation leaves its issue open, polluting the active backlog with closed work. This affects all backends, all users of the plugin. The manual workaround (`/dh:work-backlog-item resolve`) is fragile and routinely skipped, as evidenced by the discovery context.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n**Scope**: All invocations of `/complete-implementation` on issues \u2014 affects every developer using this plugin on any backend.\\n\\n**User impact**: Issues accumulate in the \\\"open\\\" state after work is completed, requiring manual cleanup. The in-progress label persists, misleading backlog readers about active work.\\n\\n**Backend impact**:\\n- GitHub: issue stays open (Fixes #NNN only works if PR is merged to default branch via GitHub merge button, not always)\\n- beads/SQLite: issue always stays open (Fixes #NNN is omitted explicitly)\\n\\n**Risk of fix**: Low \u2014 adding a terminal MCP call after verified step; no behavioral change to quality gates.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n1. Automated, backend-agnostic issue closure \u2014 no manual follow-up session required\\n2. Consistent behavior across GitHub, beads, SQLite backends\\n3. Backlog accurately reflects work state \u2014 completed items close immediately\\n4. Eliminates the fragile \\\"user runs /work-backlog-item resolve\\\" workaround\\n5. work-backlog-item auto mode step 8 (Close or resolve item) becomes redundant \u2014 potential simplification\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nAfter all quality gates pass and `status:verified` is applied:\\n1. `complete-implementation` calls `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__backlog_resolve(selector=\\\"#{issue_number}\\\", summary=\\\"Implementation complete \u2014 PR merged, AC verified PASS\\\")`\\n2. The item transitions from in-progress \u2192 resolved\\n3. The GitHub issue is closed (or equivalent per backend)\\n4. The in-progress label is removed\\n5. The `Fixes #NNN` commit annotation is preserved (GitHub UI signal \u2014 not removed, just no longer the sole closure mechanism)\\n\\nNote: `backlog_resolve` requires `summary=` (not `reason=`) \u2014 verified against `backlog_core/server.py` and ADR-9.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] After `/complete-implementation #N` completes all quality gates successfully, issue #N is closed via `backlog_resolve` MCP call\\n- [ ] The `backlog_resolve` call occurs after `status:verified` is applied and before or during the Final Step commit\\n- [ ] The call uses the correct form: `backlog_resolve(selector=\\\"#{issue_number}\\\", summary=\\\"Implementation complete \u2014 PR merged, AC verified PASS\\\")`\\n- [ ] The existing `Fixes #NNN` commit annotation behavior is preserved (not removed)\\n- [ ] Both the SAM path (plan-linked) and the Proportional Quality Gates path (issue-only) include the `backlog_resolve` call\\n- [ ] For beads backend: `backlog_resolve` executes without error (backend-agnostic protocol)\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n- `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__backlog_resolve` \u2014 MCP tool for backend-agnostic issue closure (selector, reason params)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` \u2014 target file for modification\\n- Issue #2415 / PR #2417 \u2014 reproduction context\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n**Primary target**:\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md`\\n  - Insertion point 1: After `Apply status:verified Label` section (Proportional Quality Gates path, Step 6)\\n  - Insertion point 2: After `Apply status:verified Label` section (SAM path)\\n  - The two paths share the same section name \u2014 both must be updated\\n\\n**Secondary targets** (verification only, may not need changes):\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/start.md`\\n  - Step 8 in auto mode checklist: \\\"Close or resolve item\\\" \u2014 verify if still needed after fix\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n**Blocking dependencies**: None \u2014 `backlog_resolve` is already available in the backlog MCP server.\\n\\n**Soft dependencies**:\\n- complete-implementation SKILL.md must be readable (verified present)\\n- The fix applies to both the SAM path and Proportional Quality Gates path in the skill\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\n**Estimate**: XS \u2014 1 file, 2 section insertions (SAM path + Proportional path), ~3-5 lines each\\n\\n**Complexity**: Low \u2014 no architectural change; no new tools or dependencies; straightforward text insertion at clearly identified locations in SKILL.md\\n\\n**Risk**: Low \u2014 terminal step addition; does not affect quality gate logic or issue discovery\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:3c4c73bac492b83d1610a03034210f7e -->\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/start.md` \u2014 auto mode checklist step 8: \\\"Close or resolve item\\\" \u2014 this step may become redundant or need updating\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n\\n- None \u2014 this adds a terminal step, no interface change\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\n- None identified.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (write the changed interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` \u2014 insertion point: after `Apply status:verified Label` section, one new step before `Final Step: Commit and Push`\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\n- None identified.\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 Skills Overview section references `/dh:complete-implementation` behavior\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` \u2014 if it describes issue closure steps\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] complete-implementation SKILL.md updated with backlog_resolve call\\n- [ ] work-backlog-item auto mode step 8 verified/updated (may no longer need explicit close)\\n- [ ] CLAUDE.md skills overview verified still accurate\\n- [ ] backlog-item-lifecycle.md closure step verified\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: defect\\n**Rationale**: Traceable failure with identifiable cause chain \u2014 the skill was written with GitHub-specific commit annotation for closure, but no explicit MCP-based closure step was ever added\\n**Analysis Method**: 5-whys (defect)\\n- Why is the issue open after PR merge? complete-implementation doesn't call backlog_resolve\\n- Why doesn't it call backlog_resolve? The final step only uses commit message annotation\\n- Why is commit annotation the only mechanism? It was the convention when the skill was written (GitHub-centric)\\n- Why wasn't the MCP call added later? No explicit requirement existed until issue #2415 exposed the gap\\n- Root cause: Incomplete final step \u2014 the GitHub-specific annotation was treated as sufficient\\n**Scenario Target**: Completed implementation \u2192 issue remains closed automatically via backend-agnostic MCP call\\n\\n### Root-Cause Analysis\\n\\n**Root Cause**: Missing `backlog_resolve` MCP call in `complete-implementation` final step\\n\\n**Evidence Chain**:\\n1. `complete-implementation` has a `Final Step: Commit and Push Remaining Changes` section\\n2. That section only appends `Fixes #NNN` to the commit message body (line 883)\\n3. `Fixes #NNN` is a GitHub-specific annotation with no effect on beads/SQLite backends\\n4. SKILL.md explicitly documents: \\\"omit for beads IDs \u2014 no commit-message closure\\\" \u2014 confirming awareness of the gap\\n5. No `backlog_resolve` or `backlog_close` call exists anywhere in the skill\\n6. The `backlog_resolve` MCP tool exists and is backend-agnostic (part of BacklogBackend Protocol)\\n\\n**Trigger**: Issue #2415 remained open after PR #2417 merged, exposing the gap\\n\\n**Fix**: Add `backlog_resolve(selector=\\\"#{issue_number}\\\", reason=\\\"Implementation complete \u2014 PR merged, AC verified PASS\\\")` call in the Final Step section, after status:verified is applied\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n- complete-implementation SKILL.md: primary target (add backlog_resolve call)\\n- work-backlog-item start.md: references \\\"Close or resolve item\\\" as step 8 in auto mode \u2014 will need verification after fix\\n\\n## Claim 1\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Claim**: complete-implementation applies status:verified but never closes the GitHub issue\\n**Verdict**: VERIFIED\\n**Evidence**: SKILL.md `Apply status:verified Label` section calls only `backlog_update(verified=True)` \u2014 no `backlog_resolve` or `backlog_close` call exists anywhere in the file\\n**Source**: plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md (grep confirms no backlog_resolve/backlog_close)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Claim 2\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Claim**: After PR merged the issue stays open indefinitely\\n**Verdict**: VERIFIED\\n**Evidence**: `Final Step` section only appends `Fixes #NNN` to commit body (GitHub-specific) and explicitly states \\\"omit for beads IDs \u2014 no commit-message closure\\\"\\n**Source**: plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md lines 880-884\\n</div>\\n\\n## Claim 3\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Claim**: `Fixes #NNN` annotation is GitHub-only and not backend-agnostic\\n**Verdict**: VERIFIED\\n**Evidence**: SKILL.md explicitly states \\\"omit for beads IDs \u2014 no commit-message closure\\\"; SQLite/memory backends also have no commit-message hook\\n**Source**: plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md\\n</div>\\n\\n## Claim 4\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Claim**: `backlog_resolve` is backend-agnostic\\n**Verdict**: VERIFIED\\n**Evidence**: `backlog_resolve` is part of BacklogBackend Protocol (backlog_core/backend_protocol.py); all backends (GitHub, SQLite, memory, beads) implement this Protocol\\n**Source**: plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md \u2014 Backend Providers section confirming Protocol implementations\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"3b2ce526e6da1867f84e8f4a193bfa3967503123dc89117b36fc612460056931\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCQPyQ\"}"}